<title>FRANCE: MATIF commodities volume fell in February.</title>
<headline>MATIF commodities volume fell in February.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of commodities futures and options traded on the French MATIF exchange in February fell 21.6 percent from the previous month and fell 12.4 percent compared with February 1996, MATIF said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Detailed figures for commodity contracts were as follows.</p>
<p>			 Volume    Change	Change   Open positions</p>
<p>				     on month    on year   at end-month</p>
<p> All contracts	21,862   -21.6 pct   -12.4 pct   12,604</p>
<p>  Total futures     21,862   -21.3 pct   - 6.3 pct   12,554</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>    White sugar ($) 15,771   -11.8 pct  -20.3 pct     6,952</p>
<p>    Potatoes	     252    -2.7 pct  -67.3 pct	 576</p>
<p>    Rapeseed	   4,220   -50.6 pct  +51.8 pct     3,813</p>
<p>    Wheat		1,619   +47.2 pct     N/A	  1,213</p>
<p>  Sugar options	    0  -100,0 pct     N/A	     50</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
